# Interview Training Project Rule

Use `C:/Users/lelya/Desktop/intreview_training` as the VCS root.
Use `https://github.com/Lelya-Sa/interview-training-slideshow.git` as `origin`.

At the start of work, confirm git context:
- `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`
- `git status`
- `git remote -v`

If `origin` is missing or wrong, fix it safely (no destructive commands).
Never run destructive git actions unless the user explicitly asks.

Read project structure before coding:
- Root: `package.json`, `vercel.json`, `build-direct.js`
- Client: `client/src/App.js`, `client/src/components/QuestionsView.js`
- API: `api/roadmap/summary.js`, `api/roadmap/days.js`, `api/questions.js`
- Content: `api/daily-schedule/day-NN/topics.md`, question banks under `api/**/questions.md`

Ask the user what they want to add or improve before implementing.
At prompt/chat initialization, if the user asks for a topic or learning path, first create a 3-month (12-week) job-ready schedule for that topic.
Schedule requirements:
- weekly goals for Week 1-12
- daily split: theory, coding practice, interview Q&A, revision
- milestone checkpoints every 2 weeks
- mini-project tasks
- mock interview checkpoints
- measurable weekly validation criteria ("done" definition)
- ask personalization questions: current level, hours/day, target role, deadline

Follow content/API conventions:
- `topics.md`: `### Topic Name` + `**Path**: \`../../category/subtopic/questions.md\``
- `questions.md`: `### N. Question` (or `### Question`) + `**Answer:**`
- API JSON shape: `{ success, ... }`; validate inputs; use proper 400/404/405 responses

Deployment preference:
- Vercel for frontend and lightweight serverless/proxy routes
- Railway for persistent backend services, workers, and databases
- Keep env vars clear by platform and validate end-to-end integration

Prioritize junior developer interview prep outcomes (coverage, clarity, reliability, usability).
Primary objective: user becomes job-ready in 3 months.
